1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,339
Sites use pictures, documents, audio and video.

2
00:00:04,339 --> 00:00:08,559
The Media module gives your site one library for these files.

3
00:00:08,559 --> 00:00:12,906
In this video, we see where the module lives in the admin, tour

4
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:15,930
the library, and attach a file to content.

5
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:25,112
Without a shared place for files, the same picture is uploaded again for

6
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:26,934
every page that needs it.

7
00:00:26,934 --> 00:00:31,281
Copies drift apart, nobody knows which one is current, and a file is

8
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:32,750
hard to find later.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,442
The Media module gives the site one library.

10
00:00:36,442 --> 00:00:40,915
You upload a file once, keep it in a folder, and attach it to content.

11
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:44,976
Content stores the path of the file, so every page that uses it

12
00:00:44,976 --> 00:00:46,800
points to the same place.

13
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:49,722
A file travels in three moves.

14
00:00:49,722 --> 00:00:53,826
You upload it to the library, attach it to a content item, and

15
00:00:53,826 --> 00:00:55,274
the site shows it.

16
00:00:55,274 --> 00:00:59,860
A media profile, a preset that resizes or crops an image, applies when

17
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:01,610
the theme asks for one.

18
00:01:05,887 --> 00:01:08,955
In the admin menu, Media has two pages.

19
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:14,477
Library holds the files, and Profiles holds the presets that resize images.

20
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:18,134
Profiles lists the media profiles of the site.

21
00:01:18,134 --> 00:01:22,850
This site has one, named banner, which crops an image to a wide banner.

22
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:25,851
Under Settings, Media has two entries.

23
00:01:25,851 --> 00:01:30,355
Options shows the values the library runs with, such as the allowed file

24
00:01:30,355 --> 00:01:35,495
extensions and the maximum file size, and API chooses how the library authenticates

25
00:01:35,495 --> 00:01:36,938
with the media API.

26
00:01:36,938 --> 00:01:38,960
A separate video covers both.

27
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:42,440
Tools, Features lists what a site can turn on.

28
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:46,781
Searching for media narrows the list to the features that mention it.

29
00:01:46,781 --> 00:01:49,270
Media itself is enabled on this site.

30
00:01:49,741 --> 00:01:54,545
Media Slugify rewrites the names of the folders and files you create as

31
00:01:54,545 --> 00:01:59,163
lowercase words joined by dashes, which keeps their addresses clean.

32
00:01:59,163 --> 00:02:03,781
Secure Media adds permissions that restrict access to media folders.

33
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:09,118
Other features make uploads resumable and keep every open library up to date

34
00:02:09,118 --> 00:02:11,260
when files and folders change.

35
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:16,020
Azure Media Storage and Amazon Media Storage store the files in Azure Blob

36
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:19,769
Storage or in Amazon S3, instead of on the server's disk.

37
00:02:23,999 --> 00:02:28,128
The Library page shows the folders of the site on the left, starting

38
00:02:28,128 --> 00:02:30,359
with the root folder, named Files.

39
00:02:30,845 --> 00:02:34,859
On the right, a table lists the files of the selected folder, with

40
00:02:34,859 --> 00:02:38,595
their name, the date they were last modified, and their size.

41
00:02:39,052 --> 00:02:42,466
The toolbar above the table has a button with a grid icon.

42
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:46,359
It switches the table to a grid of thumbnails, so you can recognize

43
00:02:46,359 --> 00:02:47,692
images at a glance.

44
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:50,313
Press it again to return to the table.

45
00:02:50,313 --> 00:02:54,490
The search box narrows the list to the files whose name contains what you type.

46
00:02:54,963 --> 00:02:59,362
Upload files adds files to the selected folder, and you can also drop

47
00:02:59,362 --> 00:03:00,887
files onto the page.

48
00:03:00,887 --> 00:03:05,403
A file needs an allowed extension and must not exceed the maximum size.

49
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:12,850
The menu at the end of each row offers Rename, Move, Copy, View, Download and Delete.

50
00:03:13,317 --> 00:03:15,449
Each folder has a menu too.

51
00:03:15,449 --> 00:03:20,295
Create a subfolder adds a folder inside it, and Delete is offered for

52
00:03:20,295 --> 00:03:22,557
every folder except the root.

53
00:03:26,795 --> 00:03:29,804
Content uses the library through media fields.

54
00:03:29,804 --> 00:03:34,665
This is the form that creates an Article, and its Banner Image field is empty.

55
00:03:35,164 --> 00:03:40,274
Add media opens the media picker, which shows the same library in a dialog.

56
00:03:40,735 --> 00:03:43,247
Select a file and confirm the choice.

57
00:03:43,247 --> 00:03:45,234
The field shows a thumbnail.

58
00:03:45,234 --> 00:03:49,325
When you save, the content item stores the path of the file, not

59
00:03:49,325 --> 00:03:50,435
a copy of it.

60
00:03:50,896 --> 00:03:55,051
On the site, the About page uses this same file in its Banner Image field.

61
00:03:55,051 --> 00:03:59,310
The theme requests the image through the banner profile, so the header shows

62
00:03:59,310 --> 00:04:01,076
it cropped to a wide banner.

63
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,867
That is the Media module:

64
00:04:04,867 --> 00:04:09,315
one library for the files of your site, attached to content, resized by

65
00:04:09,315 --> 00:04:12,204
profiles, and extended by optional features.

66
00:04:12,204 --> 00:04:13,706
Thanks for watching.

